Subject: [PATCH] feat(home): split the news section into Noida and Pune tabs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The homepage showed three items from the combined feed, which is how a
run of Pune stories ended up under a heading that reads as Noida news to
anyone scanning the page.

It now carries a pill switch between the two cities. Both feeds are
fetched on the server and handed to the client together, so switching is
instant — no request, no spinner, no layout shift. That matters here
because the section sits well down the page and a tab that stalls is
worse than no tab.

The 'All news' link follows the active tab to /noida-news or /pune-news
rather than the combined listing, so the section leads somewhere specific.
The switch only renders when both feeds have items; a lone tab is
decoration, not a control. Re-keying the stagger container on the active
city replays the entrance animation, so the change reads as a transition
rather than a flicker.

HomeNewsItem is a plain shape rather than a WPPost — only what the card
renders crosses the client boundary.
